  "step_3": "The decision reason requires attention to outcomes with probabilities below 20% and an adjustment of their weights in the evaluation. Only Lottery A has such an outcome (0 Euros with 10%). The individual, however, does not mention any consideration of probabilities, low-likelihood events, or weighting adjustments. Instead, the justification is purely affective and centered on a desire to take a risk. Choosing Lottery B may align with risk-taking behavior, but this does not imply use of the specific cognitive rule in the decision reason. There is no evidence that the individual considered small-probability outcomes or applied a probability transformation. The justification is incompatible with the structured, calculation-based rule of the decision reason. Therefore, it is highly unlikely that the individual used this reason.",
