{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information involves the low-probability outcomes in both lotteries: Lottery A has a -3000 Euro loss with 0.2% probability, and Lottery B has a -6000 Euro loss with 0.1% probability. Both probabilities are below 20%, so the decision reason adjusts them upward by 10 percentage points—i.e., 0.2% becomes 10.2% and 0.1% becomes 10.1%. The weighted outcomes are then calculated: for A, -3000 × 10.2% = -306; for B, -6000 × 10.1% = -606. Since -306 > -606, the decision reason would prefer Lottery A due to the more favorable (less negative) weighted outcome. Thus, the reason can be applied and favors Lottery A.",
